<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <title>Delve - Map Editor</title>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <%= csrf_meta_tags %>
    <%= csp_meta_tag %>
    <style>
      * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }
      html, body, #editor-root { width: 100%; height: 100%; }
      body { background: #14181c; color: #ddd; font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; overflow: hidden; }

      /* Row: canvas area vs. sidebar, proportional (2:1) like the class
         editor's preview/fields split. */
      .map-editor { display: flex; height: 100%; }

      .map-canvas-dropzone {
        flex: 1; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
        margin: 40px; border: 2px dashed #444; border-radius: 8px; color: #889;
      }
      .map-canvas-dropzone label { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; gap: 10px; cursor: pointer; font-size: 14px; }
      .map-canvas-error { color: #e79; font-size: 13px; padding: 8px 14px; }

      /* Column: one or two toolbar rows sit at the top of this area (row 1 -
         back/zoom - always; row 2 - replace image today, tool-mode buttons
         in later slices - only once there's something to put there); the
         pannable image fills whatever's left. */
      .map-canvas-area { flex: 2; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; }
      /* gap here is the space *between* distinct items/groups on the row
         (Back vs. the zoom group vs. whatever a later slice adds) - a
         group's own buttons stay close via .map-toolbar-button-group's own,
         tighter gap below. */
      .map-canvas-toolbar-row {
        flex: 0 0 44px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 20px; padding: 6px 14px;
        background: #1c2126; border-bottom: 1px solid #333;
      }
      /* A set of related buttons meant to read as one control (zoom
         in/fit/out today; later slices' tool-mode buttons will likely want
         this too) - reuse this instead of relying on the row's own gap. */
      .map-toolbar-button-group { display: flex; gap: 4px; }
      .map-canvas-back-link {
        color: #9ab; font-size: 13px; text-decoration: none; padding: 5px 10px;
        border: 1px solid #445; border-radius: 3px;
      }
      .map-canvas-back-link:hover { background: #234; }
      .map-canvas-toolbar-row button {
        background: #234; border: 1px solid #457; color: #9cf; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
        padding: 5px 12px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer;
      }
      .map-canvas-toolbar-row button:hover { background: #345; }
      .map-canvas-toolbar-row button:disabled { opacity: 0.4; cursor: default; }
      .map-canvas-replace { background: none; border: none; padding: 0; font-size: 12px; color: #9ab; cursor: pointer; }
      .map-canvas-replace:hover { color: #bcd; }
      .map-canvas-replace-input { display: none; }
      .map-canvas-placing-status { margin-left: auto; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; color: #fd0; }
      /* Slice 9's Simulate Units toggle - a read-only movement preview, not
         an editing tool, so it gets its own distinct (orange, matching
         MovementShapes' patrol/wander color) active state rather than the
         toolbar's usual blue. */
      .map-simulate-group button.map-simulate-active,
      .map-preview-group button.map-simulate-active { background: #532; border-color: #a72; color: #fca; }
      .map-simulate-speed { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #fca; }
      .map-simulate-notice h3 { font-size: 13px; color: #fca; font-weight: 600; }

      /* Phase 2's "walk it" 3D preview (MapPreviewCanvas) - fills the same
         slot MapCanvas's normal .map-canvas-wrapper occupies while active. */
      .map-preview-wrapper { flex: 1; min-height: 0; position: relative; background: #000; }
      .map-preview-canvas { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; cursor: grab; touch-action: none; }
      .map-preview-hint {
        position: absolute; top: 10px; left: 50%; transform: translateX(-50%);
        font-size: 12px; color: #cde; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.6); padding: 4px 10px; border-radius: 3px;
        pointer-events: none;
      }
      .map-preview-exit {
        position: absolute; top: 10px; right: 10px; background: #234; border: 1px solid #457; color: #9cf;
        font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; padding: 6px 12px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer;
      }
      .map-preview-exit:hover { background: #345; }

      .map-canvas-wrapper {
        flex: 1; min-height: 0; overflow: hidden; position: relative;
        background: #0a0c0e;
        background-image: linear-gradient(45deg, #101316 25%, transparent 25%), linear-gradient(-45deg, #101316 25%, transparent 25%), linear-gradient(45deg, transparent 75%, #101316 75%), linear-gradient(-45deg, transparent 75%, #101316 75%);
        background-size: 20px 20px;
        background-position: 0 0, 0 10px, 10px -10px, -10px 0px;
        touch-action: none;
        cursor: grab;
      }
      .map-canvas-wrapper:active { cursor: grabbing; }
      /* Placement mode (see BarriersPanel's "+" buttons): clicking sets the
         next point rather than panning, so swap the grab cursor for a
         crosshair - :active is included so a click-hold doesn't briefly
         flash back to "grabbing". */
      .map-canvas-wrapper.map-canvas-wrapper-placing,
      .map-canvas-wrapper.map-canvas-wrapper-placing:active { cursor: crosshair; }
      /* The crosshair above only wins over empty map background - an
         existing shape underneath the cursor (a barrier's line/points, a
         connection, a unit token) sets its own cursor: grab below, which
         otherwise overrides it right when precision matters most (clicking
         a new point near/against existing geometry, e.g. to snap to it).
         Higher specificity than that plain rule, so it wins while placing. */
      .map-canvas-wrapper-placing .map-canvas-shapes circle,
      .map-canvas-wrapper-placing .map-canvas-shapes line,
      .map-canvas-wrapper-placing .map-canvas-shapes image { cursor: crosshair; }
      /* will-change hints the browser to promote this to its own GPU
         compositing layer up front, so panning/zooming a large map image is
         a cheap composite instead of a full repaint of the bitmap on every
         drag frame - without it, some browsers only promote reactively
         (after the first animated frame or two), which is exactly when a
         big image visibly stutters before catching up. */
      .map-canvas-content { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; transform-origin: 0 0; will-change: transform; }
      .map-canvas-content img { display: block; user-select: none; }
      /* Same pixel-space box as the image, so its grid lines pan/zoom
         together with it for free via the shared parent's transform. */
      .map-canvas-grid { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; pointer-events: none; }
      /* Same idea, but its shapes DO take pointer events (for select/drag) -
         the SVG root stays passthrough so empty space still reaches the
         wrapper underneath for panning/add-tool clicks. */
      .map-canvas-shapes { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; pointer-events: none; }
      .map-canvas-shapes polyline, .map-canvas-shapes circle, .map-canvas-shapes line, .map-canvas-shapes image { pointer-events: auto; }
      .map-canvas-shapes circle, .map-canvas-shapes line, .map-canvas-shapes image { cursor: grab; }
      /* The 3ft hover ring around a wall point (from hovering its row in
         BarriersPanel) is a pure visual marker, not an interactive handle -
         needs to win over the plain "circle" rule above. */
      .map-canvas-shapes circle.map-canvas-point-hover-ring { pointer-events: none; cursor: default; }
      /* Group-highlight overlay (GroupShapes) - purely decorative, must
         never intercept a click meant for the real token underneath
         (grouping mode relies on that to toggle membership). */
      .map-group-highlight { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; pointer-events: none; }
      /* Movement path/zone overlay (MovementShapes) - same positioning as
         the group highlight above, but its own class since both can be
         present at once and are visually distinct (dim vs. loud). */
      .map-movement-highlight { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; pointer-events: none; }

      .map-canvas-status-bar {
        flex: 0 0 28px; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 14px; padding: 0 14px;
        background: #1c2126; border-top: 1px solid #333; color: #9ab; font-size: 12px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      }

      /* Proportional, like the class editor's preview/fields split (flex
         2:1) - there'll be a lot to show here (barriers/connections/units
         lists), so a fixed pixel width would be too cramped. */
      .map-editor-sidebar {
        flex: 1; min-width: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column;
        background: #1c2126; border-left: 1px solid #333; transition: flex-basis 0.15s ease;
      }
      .map-editor-sidebar.collapsed { flex: 0 0 36px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-toggle {
        align-self: flex-start; margin: 8px; background: #234; border: 1px solid #457; color: #9cf;
        font-size: 13px; padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer;
      }
      .map-editor-sidebar-toggle:hover { background: #345; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content { flex: 1; min-width: 0; overflow-y: auto; padding: 0 14px 14px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-placeholder { color: #778; font-size: 13px; }
      .map-sidebar-hint { color: #987; font-size: 12px; margin: 4px 0 8px; }

      /* Validate/Save controls - see client/src/validators/ValidateSaveBar.jsx,
         same markup/classes as the item/ability/class editors. */
      .save-bar { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 14px 0; }
      .save-bar .validate-button { background: #245; border: 1px solid #47a; color: #dee; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; padding: 6px 16px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; }
      .save-bar .validate-button:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #356; }
      .save-bar .validate-button:disabled { background: #333; border-color: #555; color: #888; cursor: default; }
      .save-bar .save-button { background: #2a4; border: 1px solid #4c7; color: #efe; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; padding: 6px 16px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; }
      .save-bar .save-button:hover:not(:disabled) { background: #3b5; }
      .save-bar .save-button:disabled { background: #333; border-color: #555; color: #888; cursor: default; }
      .save-bar .save-message { font-size: 12px; }
      .save-bar .save-success { color: #7c7; }
      .save-bar .save-error { color: #e79; }

      .map-editor-sidebar-content table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin-bottom: 10px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content th { text-align: left; padding: 4px 8px 4px 0; color: #9ab; font-weight: normal; white-space: nowrap; vertical-align: top; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content td { padding: 4px 0; word-break: break-word; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content input[type=number] { width: 100px; background: #111; border: 1px solid #555; color: #eee; padding: 3px 6px; border-radius: 3px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content input[type=text] { width: 100%; background: #111; border: 1px solid #555; color: #eee; padding: 3px 6px; border-radius: 3px; }
      .map-fields-dimension-pair { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
      .map-fields-dimension-pair input[type=number] { width: 70px; }

      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-block { margin: 8px 0; padding: 6px 0; border-top: 1px solid #2a2f35; border-radius: 4px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-block.map-entry-selected { background: #202832; }
      /* A not-yet-placed entry for an armed single-shot add-tool (Add
         Circle/Add Point Connection/Add Line Connection) - nothing's
         actually in mapData yet, just a cue that something's pending at
         the list position the real entry will land at once placed. */
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-block.map-entry-pending { border-top-style: dashed; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-block.map-entry-pending h3 { color: #789; font-style: italic; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-heading-row { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px; cursor: pointer; margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-heading-row h3 { font-size: 13px; color: #cce; font-weight: 600; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-heading-row h3 .map-entry-summary { font-weight: normal; color: #789; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content button.remove-entry { background: #422; border: 1px solid #644; color: #e9a; font-size: 11px; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; flex-shrink: 0; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content button.remove-entry:hover { background: #533; }
      /* A unit's editing form (table) alongside its real token, side by
         side - the token panel is a fixed-width column to the right of
         the (flexible-width) form. */
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-body { display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-body table { flex: 1; min-width: 0; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-token-panel { flex: 0 0 auto; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-token-thumb {
        width: 64px; height: 64px; border-radius: 50%; border: 1px solid #000;
        object-fit: cover; background: #223;
      }
      /* Generic heading-row summary wrapper (toggle chevron + title), so the
         remove button stays a separate flex item pinned to the far right
         via the heading row's own space-between - reused by BarriersPanel's
         per-entry collapse. */
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-row-summary { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; min-width: 0; flex: 1; }
      /* A unit's collapsed row: just its token, name, type, and a loot
         icon - the editing form/loot table only render once expanded. */
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-row-summary { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; min-width: 0; flex: 1; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-row-token { width: 22px; height: 22px; flex-shrink: 0; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-row-name { font-size: 13px; color: #cce; font-weight: 600; white-space: nowrap; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-row-type { font-size: 12px; color: #9ab; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-row-loot-icon { font-size: 12px; flex-shrink: 0; }
      /* Hovering a row (or the unit's token on the map, via hoveredIndex)
         highlights it the same way a canvas-selected entry does. */
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-block.map-unit-block.map-entry-hovered { background: #202832; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-loot-table { margin-top: 8px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-loot-table h4 { font-size: 12px; color: #9ab; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 4px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-loot-entry { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; margin: 3px 0; font-size: 12px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-loot-entry-name { flex: 1; min-width: 0; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; white-space: nowrap; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-loot-entry input[type=number] { width: 48px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-loot-entry-remove {
        background: none; border: none; color: #e9a; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1; padding: 2px 4px; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 50%;
      }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-loot-entry-remove:hover { background: #422; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-loot-count-field { font-size: 12px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-ncu-row-talk-icon { font-size: 12px; margin-left: 4px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-dialogue { margin-top: 8px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-dialogue h4 { font-size: 12px; color: #9ab; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 4px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-dialogue-line { display: flex; gap: 4px; margin: 3px 0; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-dialogue-line textarea { flex: 1; min-width: 0; font-size: 12px; resize: vertical; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-dialogue-line-buttons { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-dialogue-line-buttons button {
        background: none; border: 1px solid #445; color: #bcd; font-size: 11px; line-height: 1; padding: 2px 5px; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 3px;
      }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-dialogue-line-buttons button:disabled { opacity: 0.35; cursor: default; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-loot-count-field input[type=number] { width: 56px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-loot-count-field .map-sidebar-hint { margin: 2px 0 0; }

      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-movement-fields { margin-top: 8px; font-size: 12px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-movement-choose { display: block; margin-bottom: 6px; color: #9ab; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-movement-choose select { margin-left: 2px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-patrol-step { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; margin: 3px 0; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-patrol-step label { color: #9ab; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 3px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-patrol-step input[type=number] { width: 48px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-patrol-step-pending { color: #789; font-style: italic; font-size: 12px; margin: 3px 0; }

      /* A group is derived (units sharing a groupIdentifier), not stored -
         its block encloses member rows with a left border rather than
         looking like its own separate entry-block. */
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-block { margin: 8px 0; padding: 6px 0; border-top: 1px solid #2a2f35; border-radius: 4px; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-block.map-entry-hovered { background: #2a2016; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-header {
        display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; cursor: pointer; margin-bottom: 4px; padding: 0 2px;
      }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-name {
        flex: 1; min-width: 0; background: transparent; border: 1px solid transparent; color: #fca; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600;
        padding: 2px 4px; border-radius: 3px;
      }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-name:hover, .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-name:focus { border-color: #555; background: #111; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-count { font-size: 12px; color: #987; flex-shrink: 0; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-toggle {
        background: #333; border: 1px solid #555; color: #ccc; font-size: 11px; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; flex-shrink: 0;
      }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-toggle:hover { background: #444; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-toggle.map-unit-group-toggle-active { background: #533; border-color: #a55; color: #fca; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-members {
        margin-left: 10px; padding-left: 10px; border-left: 2px solid #543; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px;
      }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-unit-group-members .entry-block { margin: 2px 0; }
      /* While grouping mode is active, a member of the group currently
         being edited gets a distinct left accent so it reads as "in" the
         group even flat in the list (e.g. a different group's members). */
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .entry-block.map-unit-grouping-target { border-left: 3px solid #fca; padding-left: 5px; }

      .map-editor-sidebar-content .add-buttons-row { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 8px; margin: 8px 0; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content button.add-entry { background: #234; border: 1px solid #457; color: #9cf; font-size: 12px; padding: 5px 10px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content button.add-entry:hover { background: #345; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content button.add-entry:disabled { opacity: 0.4; cursor: default; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .add-buttons-row select { background: #111; border: 1px solid #555; color: #eee; font-size: 12px; padding: 4px 6px; border-radius: 3px; }
      /* "+ New Unit Type"/Refresh, same convention as UnitTypeEditor's own
         "+ New ability"/"Refresh abilities" row. */
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-sidebar-unit-type-links { font-size: 11px; color: #9ab; margin: 4px 0; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-sidebar-unit-type-links button { background: #333; border: 1px solid #555; color: #ccc; font-size: 11px; padding: 3px 8px; border-radius: 3px; cursor: pointer; }
      .map-editor-sidebar-content .map-sidebar-unit-type-links button:hover { background: #444; }
      /* A wall's points as a wrapping row of pills + "+" buttons, instead
         of one text-input row per point - positions are only ever set by
         clicking the map (placement mode) or dragging a handle on canvas,
         never typed. */
      .map-point-pills { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 4px; }
      .map-point-pill {
        display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 4px; background: #223; border: 1px solid #457;
        color: #cde; font-size: 12px; padding: 3px 4px 3px 8px; border-radius: 12px; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
      }
      .map-point-pill-pending { border-style: dashed; color: #789; }
      .map-point-pill-editable { cursor: pointer; }
      .map-point-pill-editable:hover { border-color: #9cf; color: #eef; }
      .map-point-pill-remove {
        background: none; border: none; color: #e9a; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1; padding: 2px 4px; cursor: pointer; border-radius: 50%;
      }
      .map-point-pill-remove:hover { background: #422; }
      .map-point-plus {
        background: none; border: 1px dashed #567; color: #789; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1;
        width: 20px; height: 20px; border-radius: 50%; cursor: pointer; flex-shrink: 0;
      }
      .map-point-plus:hover:not(:disabled) { color: #9cf; border-color: #9cf; }
      .map-point-plus:disabled { opacity: 0.3; cursor: default; }

      /* A collapsible section heading (Barriers today; Connections/Units
         will want this too) - starts collapsed, since a list of every
         point in every wall would otherwise dominate the sidebar. */
      .map-sidebar-section-heading { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; cursor: pointer; padding: 6px 0; }
      .map-sidebar-section-heading h3 { font-size: 13px; color: #cce; font-weight: 600; }
      .map-sidebar-section-toggle { font-size: 11px; color: #9ab; width: 1em; text-align: center; }

      @media (max-width: 700px) {
        .map-editor { flex-direction: column; }
        .map-editor-sidebar { flex: none; width: 100%; border-left: none; border-top: 1px solid #333; }
        .map-editor-sidebar.collapsed { flex: 0 0 36px; }
      }

      /* "?" hotkey help (HotkeyHelp.jsx) - a plain centered overlay, no
         existing modal component here to reuse. Escape-only dismiss (see
         MapEditor's own keydown effect), no backdrop click. */
      .map-hotkey-help-backdrop {
        position: fixed; inset: 0; background: rgba(0,0,0,0.5);
        display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; z-index: 10;
      }
      .map-hotkey-help {
        background: #1a1e22; border: 1px solid #445; border-radius: 6px;
        padding: 20px 24px; min-width: 220px;
      }
      .map-hotkey-help h3 { font-size: 14px; color: #cce; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 12px; }
      .map-hotkey-help table { border-collapse: collapse; }
      .map-hotkey-help td { padding: 4px 0; font-size: 13px; color: #ccd; }
      .map-hotkey-help td:first-child { padding-right: 14px; }
      .map-hotkey-help kbd {
        display: inline-block; min-width: 1.4em; text-align: center; background: #2a2f36;
        border: 1px solid #556; border-radius: 3px; padding: 2px 6px; font-family: inherit;
        font-size: 12px; color: #9cf;
      }
      .map-hotkey-help-hint { margin-top: 14px; font-size: 11px; color: #789; }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <%= yield %>
    <%= vite_script_tags("src/mapEditor/main.jsx", "/client/mapEditor.js") %>
  </body>
</html>
